  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223296_FY25_WFP_Somalia_Dollow Integrated Early Recovery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project overall Objective: Enhancing the food security status of the people we serve and changing their life by shifting them from high dependency of relief to early recovery through providing them the knowledge and conditional support.
 
 Outcome 1: Increased knowledge and awareness among stakeholders on the principles and standards of how to produce bread, food, and making soap and enhanced their lifestyle through shifting them from relief to early recovery status.
 
 Output 1.1: 50 vulnerable headed household women supported through domestic bakeries by receiving the knowledge and start-up kits to have their income. 
 
 Output 1.2: 100 vulnerable headed household women - benefitting from the tie and dye &amp; beauty salon 
 
 Output 1.3: 50 vulnerable household male and female have the know-how of making the soap and supported to produce it.</narrative>
  </description>
